  {
    question: 'When does General Enrollment Period (GEP) coverage start?',
    answer: 'The General Enrollment Period (GEP) runs from January 1 through March 31 each year and is for people who missed their Initial Enrollment Period and do not qualify for a Special Enrollment Period. Coverage now begins on the first day of the month following your enrollment month. The old rule forcing a wait until July 1 was eliminated by the Consolidated Appropriations Act of 2021.',
