    <h1 class="medc-h1">Medicare Effective Date Calculator: When Does Coverage Start?</h1>
    <p class="medc-date">Figures last verified against official CMS and SSA sources in {lastReviewed}.</p>

    <!-- AEO Direct Answer Block -->
    <div class="medc-aeo" role="note" aria-label="Quick Answer">
      <p class="medc-aeo-label">Quick Answer</p>
      <p class="medc-aeo-text">
        Part B starts the first day of your 65th-birthday month if you sign up in the 3 months before it. If you sign up in your birthday month or the 3 months after, it starts the first day of the next month. Premium-free Part A starts the month you turn 65 (the month before if you were born on the 1st) and can backdate up to 6 months, never before the month you turned 65.
      </p>
      <p class="medc-aeo-footer">
        Updated Oct 2026 · SSA POMS HI 00805, Medicare.gov
      </p>
    </div>

  </div>

  <!-- =======================================================
