    <DateTool client:load />
  </div>

  <RelatedToolButtons heading="Related Medicare Decision Tools" tools={relatedMedDateTools} />


  <!-- Problem Statement -->
  <p class="medc-problem">
    One of the most stressful moments of turning 65 is figuring out exactly when your Medicare coverage kicks in — especially if you are timing a retirement or transitioning off an employer health plan. Getting the date wrong by even one month can mean paying out-of-pocket for care that should have been covered. We built this calculator to give you the exact start date in seconds, based on the official SSA enrollment rules, so you can plan your transition without guessing. Once you know your start date, use our <a href="/tools/medicare-premium-calculator/">Medicare premium calculator</a> to see your exact Part A, Part B, and IRMAA costs for 2026.
  </p>

  <!-- Who This Tool Is For -->
  <ul class="medc-who" aria-label="Who this tool is for">
    <li class="medc-who-item"><span aria-hidden="true" class="medc-arrow">→</span> Adults approaching 65 who need to know their exact Medicare coverage start date before leaving employer health insurance.</li>
    <li class="medc-who-item"><span aria-hidden="true" class="medc-arrow">→</span> People born on the first of the month who want to verify whether the "born on the first" rule gives them an earlier start date.</li>
    <li class="medc-who-item"><span aria-hidden="true" class="medc-arrow">→</span> Retirees enrolling through the General Enrollment Period or Special Enrollment Period who need to verify when their doctor coverage begins.</li>
  </ul>

